# Calyx AI Platform
Kaliper competitor — pay-per-call analytics & intelligence.
May run standalone or integrated with partner stacks.

## Core Modules
- Ping Intelligence Engine (ingestion, dedup, search, bid analysis)
- Call Quality AI (transcription, scoring, sentiment)
- Financial Analytics (CPA, RPC, P&L, ROI)
- Coverage Intelligence (geo demand heatmaps)
- Audience Enrichment (500+ attributes per number)
- Ask AI (natural language reporting via pgvector + OpenAI)
- TCPA Compliance Intelligence (our unique moat — nobody has this)
- Cross-Platform Connectors (Ringba, Retreaver, TrackDrive, CallGrid)

## Tech Stack — Never suggest alternatives
- Ping ingestion: Go 1.22+
- API + business logic: Node.js + TypeScript (NestJS or Fastify)
- Frontend: React + TypeScript (Next.js)
- Real-time cache: Redis Cluster 7.x
- Message queue: Apache Kafka (AWS MSK)
- Operational DB: PostgreSQL 16
- Analytics DB: ClickHouse
- Ping search: Elasticsearch
- Transcription: Deepgram API
- AI scoring + Ask AI: OpenAI GPT-4 + pgvector
- Enrichment: EnrollHere API + Whitepages API
- Infrastructure: AWS EKS + Kubernetes + Terraform
- Observability: OpenTelemetry + Prometheus + Grafana + Loki

## Architecture Rules
- Stateless services — all session state in Redis only
- Go handles ALL real-time ping processing — never Node.js in ping path
- Kafka for all async post-processing — never block request waiting for analytics
- ClickHouse for ALL read-heavy analytics — never PostgreSQL for analytics queries
- Every table must have tenant_id from day one — never retrofit
- Separate read/write paths — write DB never used for dashboard queries
- Circuit breaker on all external deps: Go=sony/gobreaker, TS=opossum
- Multi-tenant: tenant_id on every query, PostgreSQL RLS at DB level
- Never trust tenant_id from request body — only from JWT header

## Core Principles
- DRY: extract any duplicated logic immediately
- SOLID: single responsibility, interfaces over concrete types
- KISS: simplest solution first, complexity only when performance demands
- Zero redundancy: if same code appears twice, it's wrong
- Fail fast: validate at entry point, reject early
- Fail safe: if compliance check fails → block, never allow through

## Commit Conventions (Conventional Commits)
- feat: new feature
- fix: bug fix
- perf: performance improvement
- refactor: code change with no feature/fix
- test: adding tests
- docs: documentation only
- chore: tooling, deps, config
- Keep messages under 72 characters

## What Never To Do
- Never use 'any' type in TypeScript
- Never run analytics on PostgreSQL
- Never use Node.js in ping ingestion hot path
- Never log caller ANI (phone number) in plaintext
- Never hardcode API keys or secrets in code
- Never return unbounded lists from any endpoint
- Never write blocking I/O inside a Go goroutine
- Never mix business logic with route handlers
- Never commit .env files — only .env.example
- Never skip error handling — no ignored errors ever
- Never use console.log — structured logger always